            <ArticleTitle>Pseudo-cluster-like headache secondary to contralateral epidermoid cyst of the pontocerebellar angle.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>471-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1526-4610.2007.01032.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cluster-like headaches have been described as secondary to several intracranial lesions. We report the case of a 47-year-old man who presented with a throbbing periocular pain associated with lacrimation and red eye. A contralateral epidermoid cyst was detected in the magnetic resonance imaging.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
